From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:15:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] power: reset: nvmem-reboot-mode: write the cell's own
 length again

"power: reset: reboot-mode: Add support for 64 bit magic" changed the
cell write to sizeof(u32) bytes. nvmem_cell_write() only accepts the
cell's own length (or the byte count of its bits), so a one-byte cell
now fails with -EINVAL and no reboot mode is stored any more. The PMK8850
SDAM reboot reason is such a cell (one byte, bits <1 7>): reboot to
recovery and to the boot loader would both lose their magic.

Write buf_len bytes of the 32-bit magic again and compare buf_len with
the size of that 32-bit value.

Fixes: 2257cdbe10c8 ("power: reset: reboot-mode: Add support for 64 bit magic")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c b/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
index 4479c874077c..326fe50bb1da 100644
--- a/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
+++ b/drivers/power/reset/nvmem-reboot-mode.c
@@ -37,10 +37,15 @@ static int nvmem_reboot_mode_write(struct reboot_mode_driver *reboot, u64 magic)
 		return PTR_ERR(buf);
 	kfree(buf);
 
-	if (buf_len > sizeof(magic))
+	if (buf_len > sizeof(magic_32))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	ret = nvmem_cell_write(nvmem_rbm->cell, &magic_32, sizeof(magic_32));
+	/*
+	 * The cell takes exactly its own length (nvmem_cell_write() refuses
+	 * any other); on little endian the first buf_len bytes of magic_32
+	 * are the value, as with the old unsigned int magic.
+	 */
+	ret = nvmem_cell_write(nvmem_rbm->cell, &magic_32, buf_len);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		dev_err(reboot->dev, "update reboot mode bits failed\n");
 
